The last two widgets had nowhere to live but the gallery. Cashflow is their
surface: a five-band widget card whose range control picks months or quarters,
whose hero is the cash actually collected, and whose footer states billed,
collected and outstanding. The billed series is the translucent shadow under
the collected curve, so the gap between them is the money invoiced and not
yet arrived.

The read is deliberately unfiltered and its own bounded window of 100. The
table below is a page of a filter and the chart is a claim about the ledger;
deriving the chart from the filtered page would draw a chart in which a
filter to 'paid' shows nothing ever outstanding.

compactTicks moves from the gallery fixture into lib/chart-ticks.ts, because a
tick that disagrees with its gridline is a lie about the scale and the rule
belongs to the product, not to a demo.

Seven render tests join the fourteen derivation tests. Type-checking proved
this block compiled and would have shipped it either way; rendering is what
showed the footer, the hero and the delta all carry the right figures. They
need preact-render-to-string at the root, which is the single line added to
deno.json and the single line it added to the lock." && git log --oneline -3
